WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.000
We still know very little about what's in&nbsp;
store for 2021's new "Ghostbusters" sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.400
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife," but we're&nbsp;
very excited about what's next.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.200
Here's what we know so far about director&nbsp;
Jason Reitman's foray into a new neighborhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.120
with somethin' strange.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.760
The first reports of Jason Reitman's involvement&nbsp;
in a new Ghostbusters film arrived in January&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.720
2019. Reitman soon confirmed via his Twitter&nbsp;
account that the film would hit theaters on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:32.400
July 10, 2020. Then COVID-19 happened, and&nbsp;
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife" has been moved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:39.200
back multiple times since. The film was initially&nbsp;
bumped to March 5, 2021. Then a new release date&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.360
of June 11, 2021 was set. After those both fell&nbsp;
through, Sony moved the release date back first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:52.240
to November 11, then to November 19. That would&nbsp;
seem to be the date that will finally stick.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.960
It seems like a lifetime ago now, but when&nbsp;
the initial teaser that announced the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.000
dropped in January 2019, it didn't give&nbsp;
a title. Fans simply started referring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.160
to the upcoming film as "Ghostbusters&nbsp;
2020," assuming that the movie would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.360
actually come out that year. The title&nbsp;
remained a mystery until December 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.640
when the British Board of Film Classification,&nbsp;
which has to approve all trailers in the U.K.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:22.000
revealed that the approval notice for the new&nbsp;
trailer gave the title "Ghostbusters: Afterlife."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.680
It's an appropriate title, given that the film&nbsp;
is not only about ghosts, but also about legacy.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.760
Reitman has noted that his idea for the film began&nbsp;
with a 12-year-old girl carrying a proton pack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:39.600
and that image ultimately expanded to include&nbsp;
a whole family. That 12-year-old, Phoebe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:45.200
will be played by Mckenna Grace, a rising young&nbsp;
talent who's been seen in everything from "Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.440
Marvel" to "Chilling Adventures of Sabrina"&nbsp;
to "The Haunting of Hill House." Carrie Coon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:54.960
who's shown her talents in TV series like "Fargo"&nbsp;
and "The Leftovers" as well as films like "Gone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:00.240
Girl" and "Avengers: Infinity War," plays&nbsp;
Phoebe's mother, Callie. Finn Wolfhard, who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:05.360
probably best known for "Stranger Things" and&nbsp;
the "It" movies, plays Phoebe's brother, Trevor.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.160
In September 2019, producer Ivan Reitman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.960
revealed comedy superstar turned superhero&nbsp;
Paul Rudd's role in the film, saying:

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.040
"[He's] a seismologist who's come to this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.400
small town because they've been&nbsp;
having mysterious earthquakes."

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.520
The earthquakes are likely&nbsp;
tied to paranormal events.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:25.360
Rudd's character, Mr. Grooberson, also&nbsp;
ends up working as a summer school teacher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.480
likely creating his connection with&nbsp;
the family at the film's center.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.200
In June 2019, Sigourney Weaver&nbsp;
seemed to confirm in an interview&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.280
that she was indeed reprising her&nbsp;
role as Dana Barrett. She said,

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.480
"It's going to be crazy&nbsp;
working with the guys again."

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:43.120
"Either I have a monster in my&nbsp;
kitchen or I'm completely crazy."

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.840
"I don't think you're crazy."

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.440
"Well, that makes me feel so much better."

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.800
Those "guys" are obviously Bill Murray,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.600
Dan Ayrkroyd, and Ernie Hudson. Aykroyd&nbsp;
confirmed in September 2019 that he would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:03.120
be returning to the franchise along with "most&nbsp;
of the original people." By the end of 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.600
Murray, Hudson, and Annie Potts were&nbsp;
also all confirmed to be on board.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.000
In early 2020, Vanity Fair ran a report from&nbsp;
the set of "Afterlife." While the publication&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.560
was strictly banned from revealing anything&nbsp;
about the plot, an extended conversation with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:22.240
Murray confirmed that something special was&nbsp;
in store for the iconic characters. He said,

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:27.360
"The script is good. It's got lots of&nbsp;
emotion in it. It's got lots of family in it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.720
with through lines that are really&nbsp;
interesting. It's gonna work."

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.720
Jason Reitman's feature film directorial career&nbsp;
began in 2005 with "Thank You For Smoking."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.320
Since then, he's become known for a&nbsp;
particular style that often walks the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.480
line between comedy and drama in films&nbsp;
like "Juno," "Up in the Air," "Tully,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:49.680
"Young Adult," and most recently "The Front&nbsp;
Runner." His films are often small in scale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:55.520
exploring the intimacy and absurdity of human&nbsp;
relationships rather than big set pieces.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:00.560
His comedy usually comes out of interaction&nbsp;
between characters rather than gags.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:06.080
Though he's undoubtedly formed his own writing and&nbsp;
directing style, Reitman's interest in filmmaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:12.080
has its roots in family. He's the son of actress&nbsp;
Genevieve Robert and writer/director Ivan Reitman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.920
who notably directed the original&nbsp;
"Ghostbusters" and "Ghostbusters II."

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.400
The "Ghostbusters" franchise is an integral&nbsp;
part of Jason Reitman's life. He even had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.640
a cameo in the 1989's "Ghostbusters&nbsp;
II," when he was around 11 years old.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.680
"You know, my dad says you guys are full of crap."

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.240
A sci-fi comedy about ghost hunters isn't&nbsp;
exactly in line with his previous films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:36.320
but when it was announced that he&nbsp;
would helm "Afterlife," his familial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.280
ties to the franchise helped it all make sense.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.440
It took a while to see more than a&nbsp;
few images related to Reitman's new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.360
take on "Ghostbusters," and what we&nbsp;
did see consistently leaned heavily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:52.480
on nostalgia. The first teaser begins with&nbsp;
a wide shot of a large metal building in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.120
the middle of a wooded area. The camera&nbsp;
pushes in closer and closer to the door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:02.880
eventually revealing the Ghostbusters'&nbsp;
old ride, ECTO-1, just sitting in storage.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:07.600
The first real trailer arrived in early&nbsp;
December 2019. It largely follows the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.440
kids at the heart of the story, Trevor and&nbsp;
Phoebe, as they get used to their new life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:16.000
at their inherited farmhouse in a small&nbsp;
Oklahoma town. But things get weird when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:21.040
an eerie green light starts to emit from&nbsp;
an old pit outside of town. Mr. Grooberson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:27.040
explains they're also experiencing weird seismic&nbsp;
activity that there's no logical explanation for.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:31.440
Then the kids finally bring an old ghost&nbsp;
trap they found in their farmhouse to school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:36.320
and Mr. Grooberson realizes they must&nbsp;
have a connection to the Ghostbusters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:40.880
It's revealed that there hasn't been a&nbsp;
real ghost sighting in three decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:46.880
and the Ghostbusters, once regarded as heroes,&nbsp;
are now forgotten legends. Phoebe and Trevor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:52.160
begin to seek out more information about their&nbsp;
long-lost grandfather who owned the farmhouse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:58.240
The trailer reveals he was indeed Dr. Egon&nbsp;
Spengler, one of the original Ghostbusters.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:02.240
While the trailer doesn't have any new&nbsp;
footage of the returning "Ghostbusters" cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:08.720
it does provide a nostalgia kick by playing Bill&nbsp;
Murray's speech about fate from the 1984 original.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:16.880
"Call it fate. Call it luck. Call it karma. I&nbsp;
believe that everything happens for a reason."

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:22.000
The second trailer, released in July 2021,&nbsp;
has much of the same material as the first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.360
but it does include a scene with&nbsp;
Annie Potts' Janine Melnitz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:31.360
and a quick look at the arms of what definitely&nbsp;
seems to be Dr Raymond Stantz. Ray appears to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:37.040
have some numbers tattooed on one of his arms, and&nbsp;
Jason Reitman told IGN that the numbers reference&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:41.520
the conversation about Judgment Day between&nbsp;
Ray and Winston Zeddemore from the first film.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.280
"I remember Revelation 7:12.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.720
'And I looked, as he opened the sixth seal.&nbsp;
And behold, there was a great earthquake."

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:54.160
For Jason Reitman's planned sequel, recreating&nbsp;
the same look and feel he remembered from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:58.880
original films was important. With his father's&nbsp;
connections to the beginnings of the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:04.640
he had the resources to make it all work. The&nbsp;
younger Reitman went to great lengths to replicate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:10.000
key details from the 1980s for the sequel, up to&nbsp;
and including finding the original letters used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:14.640
to make the film's posters. He explained&nbsp;
on Bill Burr's Monday Morning Podcast:

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.760
"We went back to the work files for the sound of&nbsp;
the proton pack. And we went back to the stems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:24.160
of Elmer Bernstein's score. [...] We went&nbsp;
back and found the original physical vinyl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:29.440
letters they used to create the 'Ghostbusters'&nbsp;
poster in 1984. [...] We shot physical titles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:33.920
with a light and smoke effect, because that's&nbsp;
how they would have done it back in the day."

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:37.760
When Reitman sat down with IGN to break&nbsp;
down the second trailer, he said that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:42.560
instead of trying to mimic the aesthetic of the&nbsp;
original films using modern-day visual effects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.920
he and his team went right&nbsp;
back to the source. He said,

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:52.000
"We actually found the original special effects&nbsp;
70mm footage and scanned it. We were always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:57.840
attempting to go back to the original recipe&nbsp;
and recapture as much as humanly possible."

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:01.760
That approach particularly applied&nbsp;
to the ghosts in the film. The second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:06.720
trailer contains a gang of mini Stay-Puft&nbsp;
Marshmallow Men going wild in a Walmart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:12.320
a giant spectral version of a Terror Dog,&nbsp;
and a skeletal ghost created with a puppet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:16.880
"meant to echo the taxi ghost from the&nbsp;
original," according to Reitman. He said,

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:20.640
"There's nothing like shooting with&nbsp;
practical ghosts, with having something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:23.760
right there that the actors can work with."

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:27.280
The biggest nod comes in the&nbsp;
form of new ghost Muncher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:32.240
who is similar to Slimer and pays tribute&nbsp;
to the classic character. Reitman said,

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:38.880
"The original Slimer was an angry dude and very&nbsp;
scary, and we really wanted to get back to that."

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:44.400
A complete reunion of the original four&nbsp;
Ghostbusters is sadly no longer possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:49.200
since Harold Ramis, who played Dr. Egon&nbsp;
Spengler in the first two "Ghostbusters" films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:54.160
died in 2014. His death was&nbsp;
devastating for his former castmates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:58.320
who couldn't help but feel his absence&nbsp;
while filming the latest installment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:02.640
Aykroyd, who co-wrote the original films&nbsp;
with Ramis, told Entertainment Weekly,

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:08.800
"To have that formation without that man&nbsp;
standing right there on the line with us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:14.480
was a pretty serious adjustment. He will&nbsp;
be very well represented in the new film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:18.560
I can tell you that. He's&nbsp;
very honorably represented."

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:22.960
Spengler's family honors his legacy in&nbsp;
"Ghostbusters: Afterlife," which will end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:28.080
with a dedication to the man who played him, Jason&nbsp;
Reitman confirmed to Empire magazine. He said,

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:33.120
"This movie is for my father, for my&nbsp;
daughter, and for Harold. For a long time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.800
I had the idea of a girl finding&nbsp;
a proton pack in a barn ... and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.560
just didn't know what to do with it.&nbsp;
When Harold passed all of a sudden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:46.000
I knew who she was: it was Egon's granddaughter.&nbsp;
[...] It became a Spengler story."

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:50.880
The 2016 "Ghostbusters" reboot, which&nbsp;
featured a title team of four women,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:54.800
sparked controversy virtually&nbsp;
from the moment it was announced.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.800 --> 00:10:00.320
Some longtime "Ghostbusters" fans felt that the&nbsp;
film was somehow damaging to what came before, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:06.800
a wave of social media vitriol followed throughout&nbsp;
its development and up through the film's release.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:12.000
Jason Reitman had nothing to do with that film,&nbsp;
though his father was credited as a producer.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.200
Jason Reitman's new "Ghostbusters" project&nbsp;
is a direct sequel to the original two films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:23.360
so it will ignore the reboot. That fact, plus&nbsp;
"Ghostbusters" 2016 star Leslie Jones' anger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:28.480
at being excluded from future films, meant&nbsp;
Reitman caught flak in February 2019 when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:33.120
he said that he was making an effort to,&nbsp;
quote, "hand the movie back to the fans."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:38.560
Many took his comments as an insult to&nbsp;
the 2016 movie and its cast led by women.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:42.400
Just days later, after hearing the&nbsp;
response his comments received,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:47.280
Reitman clarified his remarks, noting he&nbsp;
had, quote, "nothing but admiration" for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:52.000
the reboot and calling it an "amazing movie."&nbsp;
The director later said that "Ghostbusters:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:57.440
Afterlife" was actually inspired by the&nbsp;
2016 film in a way. He told SFX Magazine,

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:02.240
"I think that the remake proved, at least to&nbsp;
me, the idea that the Ghostbusters could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:07.280
anyone, and I expanded on this idea with&nbsp;
'Afterlife' while always focusing on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:11.200
family aspect and the history that&nbsp;
was created by the original films."

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.320
"Are you the Ghostbusters?"

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:15.680
"Actually, we're the conductors of the--"

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.840
"Yes. We're the Ghostbusters."

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:23.360
Dan Aykroyd in particular had been trying to get&nbsp;
the "Ghostbusters" series back on the big screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:28.240
years before the 2016 reboot, and it does&nbsp;
seem that the door is now open to some ideas.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:33.440
Those ideas apparently include a prequel&nbsp;
called "Ghostbusters High," which Aykroyd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:38.480
has written as a potential feature film that&nbsp;
could launch a TV series chronicling how Peter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:44.880
Ray and Egon first met as teenagers in 1969 in&nbsp;
New Jersey. Though he was excited about the idea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:50.480
Aykroyd also cautioned that "Ghostbusters&nbsp;
High" is just one of a number of ideas he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:54.160
and the Reitmans are exploring. Aykroyd&nbsp;
explained to The Canadian Press,

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:58.480
"We have other stuff after the Jason&nbsp;
Reitman-helmed movie. We have at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:03.840
one or two other concepts for the Ghostbusters,&nbsp;
and then we'll look at doing the prequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:08.080
which will be a perfect button on&nbsp;
all we've done up to that point."

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:11.440
In other words, if you like&nbsp;
"Ghostbusters," just keep an eye out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:14.960
because we seem to be far from&nbsp;
finished with the franchise.

